WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:16.300
something happened on Christmas Eve in
1914 in the trenches World War one

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:25.130
during the Battle of Ypres and world war
one was the most sickening of wars as

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:34.659
far as I can tell a world of death and
destruction and fire and pain and mud

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:43.249
and suffering and as the British
prepared for an attack that Christmas

00:00:43.249 --> 00:00:50.899
Eve they heard the Germans their enemy
across the way and they heard the

00:00:50.899 --> 00:01:01.159
Germans laughing and singing Christmas
carols and eventually the Germans called

00:01:01.159 --> 00:01:09.590
out come on over Tommy which is slang
for a British soldier and they said we

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:21.160
won't fire at you and eventually the
British cautiously started to head over

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:25.790
and the Germans came out and started to
head over they head toward each other

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:36.830
and eventually they all met in no-man's
land when they got there they talked and

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:42.770
they laughed and they sang and they
joked and they told stories and the

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:54.280
legend is that they even played some
soccer and most important at that moment

00:01:54.280 --> 00:02:03.880
they saw each other as humans as fellow
human beings

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:15.200
and eventually as the morning came on
they all went back to their trenches and

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:20.960
when they got back to their trenches
they put down their weapons they sat

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:32.330
there and they they yelled jokes back
and forth and they in fight and for a

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:42.890
couple days there was peace and the
soldiers thought to themselves what are

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:51.610
we even fighting for how did we end up
here and why are we killing each other

00:02:53.560 --> 00:03:01.040
and these soldiers on both sides the
Germans and the British realized that

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:14.330
there supposedly monstrous enemy they
were just other men other men with

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:19.250
different backgrounds and different
cultures and different languages but

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:30.920
they realized that their enemy were just
men like them they realized that they

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:42.650
were all people and on the third day the
Germans were ordered from High Command

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:50.959
to shoot their machine guns and so the
Germans told the British what time they

00:03:50.959 --> 00:03:54.980
were gonna shoot and they said they were
gonna shoot high so the British should

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:59.630
get low and take cover around that
certain time to make sure nobody got

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:09.350
hurt and that's what happened
the Germans shot high and no one got

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:16.669
hurt in another couple of days of peace
went by but then an order came from the

00:04:16.669 --> 00:04:21.690
British headquarters
and it said that anyone found

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:28.360
fraternizing with the enemy would be
court-martialed and if they were not

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:34.530
fighting the enemy and they were found
guilty of that they would be executed

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:52.860
and the generals got their way they got
what they wanted and that night the war

00:04:52.860 --> 00:05:02.500
the horrendous war on that patch of land
commenced again and the bombs and the

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:07.410
mortars and the fire and the bullets

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:13.830
they all came to extract their toll and

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:22.979
destroy and maim and kill these men on
both sides

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:34.680
and that is an awful end to a beautiful
story it takes that beautiful story and

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:38.000
turns it into a nightmare

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:54.780
but in that story there's a glimpse of
hope the hope is that we as human beings

00:05:54.780 --> 00:06:04.260
can see other people as human beings and
then know we can and I know it's not

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:15.510
always easy but we need to do this on
both sides of the trenches and if you're

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:20.930
a protester looking at a police officer
or looking at a National Guard soldier

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:26.730
please take a moment to remember that
that police officer or that soldier is a

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:33.980
son or a father or a mother or a
daughter or a brother or a sister

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:45.750
remember that that soldier or that
officer is a person and if you are a

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:52.830
police officer or you're a soldier and
you're looking at a protester or even a

00:06:52.830 --> 00:07:02.750
rioter please please remember the same
thing that you are looking at a person a

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:11.820
person like you a person with a family a
person with aspirations a person with

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:18.180
hope a person with pain and sadness and
joy and misery a person with hate and a

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:21.470
person with love

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:42.420
a person like you look it can be easy to
dehumanize others and when we determine

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:52.410
eyes we separate people from who we are
from what we are and it becomes easy to

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:57.419
hate them because they are different
from us well I'm telling you they are

00:07:57.419 --> 00:08:12.510
not that different the person you are
looking at that is a person and yes

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:17.370
they're angry and yes they're frustrated
yes they're scared and they're tired and

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:27.330
they're fed up and they're aggravated
and they're full of potential and they

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:41.570
are deeply flawed in other words they
are a person just like you

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:49.880
please remember that be safe out there

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.870
and try to take care of one another

